// Title: VsCode Powershell Profile Modification
// Sigma ID: 3a9fa2ec-30bc-4ebd-b49e-7c9cff225502
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-24 | Modified: 2023-01-06
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546.013
// Description: Detects the creation or modification of a vscode related powershell profile which could indicate
//   suspicious activity as the profile can be used as a mean of persistence
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the profile by developers or administrators
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_profiles?view=powershell-7.2
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_vscode_powershell_profile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft.VSCode_profile.ps1"
